## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Piyrox project.

### Changes Made

**1. Installed Package:**
- Added `@vercel/analytics` package to dependencies using npm
- Package version installed as per latest available on npm registry

**2. Modified Files:**

**`package.json`:**
- Added `@vercel/analytics` to the dependencies section

**`package-lock.json`:**
- Updated with new dependency tree for @vercel/analytics and its transitive dependencies

**`src/app/layout.tsx`:**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, placed after the `<CustomerAIChat />` component

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Web Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the Next.js App Router specific integration:

1. **Framework Detection:** Identified this as a Next.js 14.2.5 project using the App Router architecture (src/app directory structure)

2. **Package Manager:** Detected npm as the package manager (package-lock.json present)

3. **Integration Point:** Added the Analytics component to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`), which is the recommended approach for Next.js App Router projects. This ensures analytics tracking is available across all pages.

4. **Component Placement:** Positioned the `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body, after existing components, to avoid blocking render and maintain the existing component hierarchy.

### Testing

- ✅ Build completed successfully with `npm run build`
- ✅ No TypeScript compilation errors
- ✅ Analytics component properly imported and integrated
- ⚠️ ESLint configuration not present in project (requires separate setup)

### Next Steps (for project maintainers)

To enable Web Analytics tracking:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
3. Verify functionality by checking browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view` when visiting pages

### Notes

- The Analytics component uses the `@vercel/analytics/next` import which provides seamless Next.js integration with automatic route tracking
- No environment variables or additional configuration required
- Analytics data will only be collected when deployed to Vercel or when running with Vercel CLI
- The existing Ahrefs analytics script in the layout remains unchanged and will continue to work alongside Vercel Analytics
